{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 44,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have heard with our ears, O God,\nOur fathers have told us,\nWhat work thou didst in their days,\nIn the days of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst drive out the nations with thy hand;\nBut them thou didst plant:\nThou didst afflict the peoples;\nBut them thou didst spread abroad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they gat not the land in possession by their own sword,\nNeither did their own arm save them;\nBut thy right hand, and thine arm, and the light of thy countenance,\nBecause thou wast favorable unto them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art my King, O God:\nCommand deliverance for Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Through thee will we push down our adversaries:\nThrough thy name will we tread them under that rise up against us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I will not trust in my bow,\nNeither shall my sword save me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou hast saved us from our adversaries,\nAnd hast put them to shame that hate us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In God have we made our boast all the day long,\nAnd we will give thanks unto thy name for ever. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now thou hast cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " off, and brought us to dishonor,\nAnd goest not forth with our hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest us to turn back from the adversary;\nAnd they that hate us take spoil for themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast made us like sheep ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "appointed",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for food,\nAnd hast scattered us among the nations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou sellest thy people for nought,\nAnd hast not increased ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy wealth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by their price.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbors,\nA scoffing and a derision to them that are round about us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest us a byword among the nations,\nA shaking of the head among the peoples.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the day long is my dishonor before me,\nAnd the shame of my face hath covered me,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the voice of him that reproacheth and blasphemeth,\nBy reason of the enemy and the avenger.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All this is come upon us; yet have we not forgotten thee,\nNeither have we dealt falsely in thy covenant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our heart is not turned back,\nNeither have our steps declined from thy way,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That thou hast sore broken us in the place of jackals,\nAnd covered us with the shadow of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If we have forgotten the name of our God,\nOr spread forth our hands to a strange god;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will not God search this out?\nFor he knoweth the secrets of the heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea, for thy sake are we killed all the day long;\nWe are accounted as sheep for the slaughter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Awake, why sleepest thou, O Lord?\nArise, cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not off for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore hidest thou thy face,\nAnd forgettest our affliction and our oppression?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For our soul is bowed down to the dust:\nOur body cleaveth unto the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.44.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rise up for our help,\nAnd redeem us for thy lovingkindness’ sake.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "Former deliverances and present troubles.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of the sons of Korah. Maschil.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
